window.PET_DATA["knowledge/grammar-04-reported-speech.json"] = {"id":"grammar-04","type":"grammar","title":"Reported Speech","objective":"Report statements and questions with correct backshift and word order.","sections":[{"heading":"Statements: backshift","body":"When the reporting verb is in the past (`said, told`), the original tense moves one step into the past:\nPresent Simple → Past Simple: `I like tea` → `She said she liked tea.`\nPresent Continuous → Past Continuous: `I'm working` → `He said he was working.`\nPast Simple → Past Perfect: `I arrived late` → `She said she had arrived late.`\nwill → would: `I'll help` → `He said he would help.`","bodyZh":"转述动词为过去时（said, told）时，原句时态后退一步：一般现在→一般过去；现在进行→过去进行；一般过去→过去完成；will→would。","examples":[{"en":"\"I am tired.\" → She said (that) she was tired.","zh":"「我累了。」→ 她说她累了。"},{"en":"\"We will visit Rome.\" → They said they would visit Rome.","zh":"「我们会去罗马。」→ 他们说他们会去罗马。"}],"tip":"`that` is optional: `She said she was tired` is perfect."},{"heading":"Questions","body":"Reported questions use **statement word order** (subject before verb) and no `do/does/did`:\n`Where do you live?` → `He asked me where I lived.`\nYes/no questions use `if` or `whether`: `Are you hungry?` → `She asked if I was hungry.`","bodyZh":"转述疑问句用陈述语序（主语在动词前），不用 do/does/did；一般疑问句用 if 或 whether。","examples":[{"en":"\"What time is it?\" → He asked what time it was.","zh":"「几点了？」→ 他问几点了。"},{"en":"\"Can you swim?\" → She asked me if I could swim.","zh":"「你会游泳吗？」→ 她问我是否会游泳。"}],"tip":"The word-order mistake (`he asked where did I live`) is one of the most common PET errors. Practise it!"},{"heading":"say / tell & commands","body":"`tell` needs a person: `She told me...` (not 'She told to me' / 'She said me').\nCommands use `to + infinitive`: `Sit down!` → `The teacher told us to sit down.`\nNegative: `not to + infinitive`: `Don't be late!` → `Mum told me not to be late.`","bodyZh":"tell 后必须接人：She told me...；命令句用 to + 动词原形，否定用 not to。","examples":[{"en":"He told us to wait outside.","zh":"他叫我们在外面等。"},{"en":"The doctor told her not to eat too much sugar.","zh":"医生叫她不要吃太多糖。"}],"tip":"say something / tell somebody — memorise this pair."}],"commonErrors":[{"wrong":"She said me she was tired.","right":"She told me she was tired.","why":"'say' cannot take a person directly; use 'tell + person'."},{"wrong":"He asked where do I live.","right":"He asked where I lived.","why":"Reported questions use statement word order, no 'do'."},{"wrong":"She told to me the news.","right":"She told me the news.","why":"'tell' takes the person without 'to'."}],"summary":{"keyPoints":["Backshift: present → past, will → would, can → could.","Reported questions: statement word order, if/whether for yes/no.","tell + person · say + (that) clause.","Commands: told somebody (not) to do something."],"mustKnow":["said (that)","told me to","asked if","asked where I lived"]},"linkedPractice":["reading"],"reviewItems":[]};
